# Agent routing (shipyard)

If `docs/agents/shipyard.md` is missing, do not assume surfaces or QA commands. Tell the user to run `/setup-shipyard`.

## Invariant: writer ≠ reviewer

- **Writers** never run `/code-review`, never commit, never declare the work done, never review their own diff in the same context.
  - Composer (`implementer`, `frontend-developer`): Matt `/implement` → `/tdd`.
  - Grok (`designer` as writer): writes only `design-system/**` — does not run `/implement`.
- **Reviewers** (Grok) are read-only. They report findings; they do not edit product code.
- The orchestrator launches reviewers in **fresh context** after the writer finishes.
- Never use `inherit` model from writer → reviewer.
- When `Surface: design-system`, the writer was `designer` — **do not** launch `designer` as the Design review axis (spec + standards cover MASTER fidelity). Launch `designer` as Design reviewer only when the writer was not `designer` and the overlay visual pack is on.

## Invariant: ticket author ≠ readiness gate

- **`planner`** (and anyone who drafted the ticket) never sets `ready-for-agent` and never runs the CORE gate on their own draft in the same context.
- **`ticket-readiness-reviewer`** runs in **fresh** Grok context after refine (batches of 1–5 tickets from the same tree, independent verdicts). Only a `READY` verdict authorizes `**Status:** ready-for-agent`.
- Never use `inherit` model from planner → ticket-readiness-reviewer.
- Draft tickets stay at `needs-info` until the gate passes.

## Models (Cursor only)

| Role | Model |
| --- | --- |
| `implementer`, `frontend-developer` | `composer-2.5` |
| `planner`, `designer`, `copywriter`, orchestrator, all reviewers, `ticket-readiness-reviewer`, `qa-verifier` | `cursor-grok-4.6-high` |
| Claude / GPT | do not use |

## Ticket `Surface:` → writer

| Surface | Writer |
| --- | --- |
| `backend` | `implementer` |
| `frontend` | `frontend-developer` |
| `design-system` | `designer` |
| `tooling` | `implementer` |

Every ticket under `.scratch/<feature>/issues/` must declare **`Surface:`**. `Surface:` is routing metadata **after** a justified split (blocked-ness → proof unit → ownership) — not the primary split reason. Paths each writer owns come from `docs/agents/shipyard.md`. If `visual: off`, do not use `frontend` or `design-system`. Never invent `fullstack`.

## Commands

| Command | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `/setup-shipyard` | Overlay + `scripts/sync-cursor.sh` (once per repo) |
| `/update-shipyard` | Pull submodule + re-materialize kernel and packs |
| `/plan-work` | Idea → always grill → inventory → shape A–E + Lane → draft → preflight → batched readiness gate → tickets. PRD only for D/E. No product code. `/plan-prd` is an alias. |
| `/refine-ticket` | Refine one `.scratch` issue + fresh readiness gate |
| `/ship-ticket` | Branch `feat/<feature>/<NN>-<slug>` → plan gate → writer by `Surface:` → review matrix → QA ticket/increment → livingdocs on contract close → commit |
| `/ship-prd` | Branch `feat/<feature>` → tickets **serially** (one writer) → increment QA at end |
| `/review-diff` | Review battery + QA only, no writer |
| `/audit-ui` | Only if visual on. Report → `.scratch/<audit-slug>/AUDIT.md`. No `src/` edits. |

## Agent → when to use

| Agent | When |
| --- | --- |
| `planner` | `/plan-work` (alias `/plan-prd`), `/refine-ticket` draft/refine, seams — never self-certify ready |
| `ticket-readiness-reviewer` | After draft/refine + preflight — CORE gate; batches of 1–5 same tree; only READY → `ready-for-agent` |
| `implementer` | `Surface: backend` or `tooling` |
| `frontend-developer` | `Surface: frontend` (visual pack) |
| `designer` | `Surface: design-system`; UI review; `/audit-ui`; `/plan-work` only when a reusable visual contract changes |
| `copywriter` | Visible strings when copy pack is on |
| `spec-reviewer` | After writer — diff vs ticket AC / `Done means:` / Out of scope |
| `standards-reviewer` | After writer — `.cursor/rules` + smells (`standard`/`high`; light uses static lints) |
| `security-reviewer` | After writer — **high** always; else auth, input, secrets, RLS per diff |
| `database-reviewer` | Overlay `database: on` and diff matches SQL globs |
| `qa-verifier` | Overlay QA: scope `ticket` or `increment` |

## Review matrix (ship / review-diff)

Launch in fresh Grok context. Read ticket `**Lane:**` (missing → `standard`).

| Axis | Agent | When |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Spec | `spec-reviewer` | always |
| Standards | `standards-reviewer` | `standard` and `high`. **light:** static lints only |
| Security | `security-reviewer` | `high` always; else diff touches auth, external input, permissions, secrets, or SQL/Supabase/RLS globs |
| Database | `database-reviewer` | overlay `database: on` and diff matches SQL globs |
| Copy | `copywriter` | Copy pack on and visible user-facing strings changed |
| Design | `designer` | Visual pack on, UI/css/DS changed, **and** writer was not `designer` |

Do not skip an axis the matrix requires. Do not launch an axis it does not.

Fix loop: copy/UI → `frontend-developer`; DS gap → `designer` then frontend; domain/SQL/tooling → `implementer`.

## Skills

- **Process (Matt, global):** `/ask-matt`, `/grill-with-docs`, `/to-spec`, `/to-tickets`, `/implement`, `/tdd`, `/code-review`
- **Ticket craft:** plugin `agent-ready` (anatomy, slicing, refinement, CORE gate)
- **Docs:** `/livingdocs-record` at contract close (last ticket of a tree, or tree without PRD)
- **QA:** plugin `verification-loop` — overlay QA ticket vs increment
- **Stack / visual:** copied into `.cursor/skills/` by `scripts/sync-cursor.sh`

## Issue tracker

Ship tickets live under `.scratch/<feature>/issues/` even if Matt `/triage` uses GitHub. See `docs/agents/issue-tracker.md`.

## Git

`docs/agents/git-conventions.md`. Never ship on the overlay base branch (default `main`). Do not force-push or amend commits already pushed.
